  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating and comparing the variances of the lotteries and preferring the one with smaller variance (Lottery B). However, the individual only refers to expected values and makes their decision based on which lottery offers a higher expected gain (Lottery A). The information relevant to the decision reason (variance) is not considered in the verbal report. Furthermore, the individual’s justification (higher expected value) aligns with an expected value maximization rule, not a variance-minimization rule. There is no indication that variance or risk was part of the deliberation. Therefore, it is certain that the decision reason (based on variance) was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
